WEBVTT

00:15:56.396 --> 00:16:01.076
and we probably overestimate
the degree of similarity

00:16:01.116 --> 00:16:02.556
between our perceptual worlds,

00:16:02.596 --> 00:16:05.796
because they're all filtered
through language.

00:16:05.796 --> 00:16:09.036
I mean, I just used the word “red,”
and there are many shades of red;

00:16:09.076 --> 00:16:10.996
painters would say, "What red?"

00:16:10.996 --> 00:16:13.076
I remember when I was decorating my house,

00:16:13.076 --> 00:16:15.476
it's like, "I want to paint
the walls white."

00:16:15.516 --> 00:16:18.076
How many shades of white are there?

00:16:18.116 --> 00:16:19.796
This is too many.

00:16:19.836 --> 00:16:21.996
And they have weird names,
which doesn't help.

00:16:22.036 --> 00:16:25.956
We will overestimate
the similarity of our universe.

00:16:25.956 --> 00:16:28.316
And I think it's a really
interesting question,

00:16:28.316 --> 00:16:30.116
how much they do indeed diverge.